  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "T//8kXBDbLQ1QNIT0d3xIBVHuPM=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:28:27.569Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Valantic has won an OutSystems EMEA Partner Impact Award and, per the record, buys low-code specialists \u2014 its acquisition of Do iT Lean, a Portuguese Elite and Premier OutSystems partner, closed in November 2022. The screen's reading is that this makes it a potential acquirer as much as a partner.\n\nThat is a distinct disqualifier from the slot-occupancy verdicts elsewhere in the cohort, and a more interesting one. An acquisitive platform consolidator does not evaluate a new capability as something to carry to its clients; it evaluates it as an asset to own, or as a competitor to a practice it has just paid for. The conversation shifts from partnership terms to valuation, and the counterparty's incentive is to acquire the capability rather than to distribute it.\n\nThe OutSystems award compounds this, since the acquired capability being consolidated is precisely the proprietary app-layer position the thesis has to displace. Valantic is therefore filed do-not-pitch on both grounds at once \u2014 the slot is occupied, and the firm's growth pattern makes it a buyer rather than a channel.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**9 \u00b7 do not pitch**\n- Valantic (DE)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Won an OutSystems EMEA Partner Impact Award. Buys low-code specialists - so a potential acquirer as much as a partner.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:28:27.569351Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:28:27.569355Z"
    }
  },
